# Files excluded from the Vercel deployment.
#
# Probably Weather is a zero-build static deploy: each deploy uploads the repo
# minus the patterns below, and whatever is uploaded is what the site serves at
# its root. Before this file existed, internal docs were publicly fetchable
# (audit 2026-05-31, FIX 1: /CLAUDE.md, /AUDIT_REPORT.md,
# /PROBABLY_WEATHER_MONETISATION_INFRA_REPORT.md, /lighthouse-report.json all
# returned 200 on prod). These are info-disclosure, not secrets (no tokens are
# committed; keys live in env vars).
#
# SAFE-TO-EXCLUDE check: the running site serves only HTML pages
# (index.html, install.html, privacy.html), assets/**, api/**, og/**,
# manifest.json, sw.js, vercel.json, and .well-known/** — NONE of which is a
# .md file, so excluding all markdown cannot drop a user-facing page. The only
# in-repo .md reference is a code comment (app.js → docs/picker-rotation-logic.md),
# not a runtime fetch.

# Internal planning / audit / review / ship-notes docs — all markdown, none served.
*.md
docs/

# …except the two docs tests/product-spine.test.js reads. Since the release
# gate (package.json build → vitest run) the suite runs in the build container,
# so these are BUILD-INPUT. Re-including them is not a disclosure regression:
# outputDirectory is dist/, and dist/ holds only STATIC_ENTRIES
# (scripts/build.mjs) — nothing at the repo root is served any more.
!PRODUCT_SPINE.md
!DESIGN_DOSSIER_probably-weather_2026-07-14.md

# Lighthouse report artifact.
lighthouse-report.json

# Stray MyChannel screenshots accidentally dropped into this repo.
mc-*.png

# Internal tooling — committed but never runtime-served. The OG generator
# under tools/ is run locally; its output (og/*.jpg) is committed separately
# and served from og/.
# NOTE: scripts/ is NOT excluded any more — the Group 6 build pipeline
# (buildCommand: npm run build → scripts/build.mjs) runs in Vercel's build
# container and needs it uploaded. It is build-input, not deploy output:
# only dist/ is served.
tools/
.claude/
.github/

# Eval harness — was publicly fetchable on prod (verified 2026-06-11:
# /tests/home-name.test.js returned 200). Same info-disclosure class as the
# *.md exclusion above. Nothing at runtime imports from eval/.
#
# NOTE: tests/ is NOT excluded any more, for the same reason scripts/ isn't.
# The release gate runs the suite INSIDE the build (package.json build →
# `vitest run && …`), so tests/ is build-input; leaving it out made vitest
# exit 1 with "No test files found" and would have broken every deploy. The
# 2026-06-11 disclosure is already closed by a different mechanism: the deploy
# now serves dist/ (outputDirectory in vercel.json), and scripts/build.mjs
# copies only STATIC_ENTRIES into it — tests/ is never served regardless.
eval/
